</div>
<h2 id="start">The Rookie Start</h2>
<p>Cleveland's second-round pick has scored a touchdown in each of his first two career games, capped by a five-catch, 95-yard, one-touchdown performance against Tampa Bay in Week 2 — the best game by any rookie receiver so far this season. Boston was Washington's leading receiver in 2025 with 62 catches for 881 yards and 11 touchdowns, built almost entirely on contested catches and size mismatches rather than separation speed, and that profile has translated immediately to the NFL.</p>
