<h2 id="combine">The Test He Skipped, Twice</h2>
<p>Boston never ran the 40-yard dash at the 2026 NFL Combine, and then, on the advice of his agent, skipped it again at Washington's pro day — an unusual decision even by the standards of receivers who sit out one workout or the other. What he did do instead was jump: a 35-inch vertical at the combine, improved to 37.5 inches at his pro day, alongside a 6.80-second 3-cone and a 4.28-second shuttle.</p>
